```java
public class Fibbo {
    private int a = 0;
    private int b = 1;

    public int next(int num) {
        if (num == 0) {
            return a;
        }
        if (num == 1) {
            return b;
        }
        for (int i = 2; i <= num; i++) {
            int temp = a;
            a = b;
            b = temp + b;
        }
        return b;
    }
}
```

In this class, we maintain two instance variables `a` and `b` to keep track of the last two numbers in the Fibonacci sequence. The `next` method generates the next number in the sequence by adding the last two numbers.

